@style(IDocDemo)
@title(The course file and Docent)

A course is a file and a folder. The file, PHY101.course beside this one, is the syllabus and the gradebook's rules in one text. Docent is the course page that file drives: students see their to-do list, work and marks there; teachers see the roster, the gradebook and the marking queue.

@box(w=100%, style=offline)
Publishing, the gradebook and marking run on the IDoc server; the course file can be read and edited anywhere.
@end

@section(Reading PHY101.course)

Open @link(PHY101.course, PHY101.course) and read it top to bottom. Each line is one fact:

@dl
course: names the course, its title and term.
staff, teacher, ta, grader: who teaches and who marks. observers: which page an observer gets.
meet, hours: the online meeting links and bookable office hours.
weights, drop, scale, late: what the grade is made of, which low scores drop, the letter cut-offs and the late policy.
grading: how marking is divided (split=wrong deals one task per wrong answer; split=paper deals whole papers).
groups: named student groups, marked once per group.
outcome: what students should be able to do; work tagged outcomes= counts towards it.
topic, week, unit: a block of the course, running until the next one.
read: ungraded reading. assign: work to hand in. exam: a timed paper. discuss: a graded discussion. tool: an outside LTI tool.
provide: files that land in each student's workspace (when=auto copies them at once).
gate: what a student must reach before the next topic opens.
@end

@section(Publishing to the course)

A document reaches a class through one line in the course file: add @@assign or @@exam naming it, save, and Docent publishes a snapshot. Editing the source afterwards does not change a paper somebody is sitting; publish again to send a new version.

@section(Teaching live)

Open a document in the editor and press the teach shortcut (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+M) to open it to the class. A studio or question with time= stays open for that long once the teacher opens it, for example:

@q(fn: 4, id=live-q1) What is 2 + 2?

@section(Course defaults)

A teacher's usual lines (weights, late policy, scale) are saved as defaults and stamped into a new course file with a checklist of what changed.
